 "c_sql": {
  "cat": "code",
  "prompt": "Write a SQL query selecting the name and salary of the top 3 highest-paid employees from a table 'employees(name, salary)'.",
  "answer": "# SQL Query: Top 3 Highest-Paid Employees\n\n## Standard SQL (works in most databases)\n\n```sql\nSELECT name, salary\nFROM employees\nORDER BY salary DESC\nLIMIT 3;\n```\n\n## Database-Specific Variations\n\n### SQL Server / MS SQL\n```sql\nSELECT TOP 3 name, salary\nFROM employees\nORDER BY salary DESC;\n```\n\n### Oracle (older versions)\n```sql\nSELECT name, salary\nFROM (\n    SELECT name, salary\n    FROM employees\n    ORDER BY salary DESC\n)\nWHERE ROWNUM <= 3;\n```\n\n### Using Window Functions (handles ties consistently)\n```sql\nSELECT name, salary\nFROM (\n    SELECT name, salary,\n           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY salary DESC) AS rn\n    FROM employees\n) ranked\nWHERE rn <= 3;\n```\n\n## Notes on Handling Ties\n\n- **`LIMIT 3` / `TOP 3`** \u2014 Returns exactly 3 rows, arbitrarily breaking ties.\n- **`RANK()`** \u2014 Returns all employees tied at the 3rd-highest salary (may return more than 3 rows):\n  ```sql\n  SELECT name, salary\n  FROM (\n      SELECT name, salary,\n             RANK() OVER (ORDER BY salary DESC) AS rnk\n      FROM employees\n  ) ranked\n  WHERE rnk <= 3;\n  ```\n- **`DENSE_RANK()`**",
